{"seq": 6, "actor": "emmy", "kind": "correction", "standing": "current", "text": "Refining inherited branch-3 #94/#98/#101 reporting limitation using joint #4: cell41 panels G/H are saved author-pipeline selected-network outputs. Reordered-path reconstructions RBFENN (R,MUE,tau)=(0.77,0.67,0.55), LOMAP=(0.77,0.66,0.57), offset=(0.88,0.49,0.70) agree with that raster within the stated digitisation uncertainty. The FC prose at branches/branch-3/inputs/Q.txt:812-813 corresponds to cell55 printed lower components (0.67,0.75,0.43), whereas the FC figure bars correspond to medians about (0.694,0.769,0.467). Q therefore quotes different summary components for FC between this prose and saved figure. The approximate prose MUE0.55 at :863-864 matches neither RBFENN/LOMAP bars near0.66-0.67 nor offset near0.49; its sentence can refer to RBFENN/LOMAP results or to offset. This is a prose-versus-saved-notebook discrepancy, not an error claim about an uninspected typeset figure. It does not change recovered graph identity or six-decimal ligand fits."}
{"seq": 8, "actor": "ada", "kind": "finding", "standing": "current", "text": "New conditional resource construction: ada/loading_cost_audit.py compiles two function-preserving real-overlap routes for a synthetic nonnegative 187-vector and signed real 187-weight row, padded to 256 amplitudes on eight data qubits plus ancilla. PennyLane 0.45.1 / NumPy 2.4.6, seed 20261007, elementary RX/RY/RZ/PhaseShift/H/X/Z/CNOT basis, no optimisation or routing. P input-preparation routing uses 6294 CNOTs; the equivalent zero-start controlled \\(U_x^\\dagger U_w\\) route uses 6040 CNOTs per shot. Gate-by-gate algebraic simulation verifies both ancilla means against the real dot product within \\(6\\times10^{-15}\\). A P three-layer restricted row instead uses 2480 CNOTs in this compilation but changes the weight family (72 angles versus an arbitrary 187-row). This is not a minimum-gate theorem, device timing or compilation of historical activations. For all 45 models and 120 edges, direct final-row evaluation takes 1009800 multiply-adds; the unoptimised zero-start circuit uses 32616000 CNOTs even at one shot per model/edge. The local synthetic NumPy batch dot products took median 0.000301 seconds over 100 timings, excluding encoders and all training; that is an indicative CPU component measurement, not an optimised end-to-end speed comparison. Counts multiply by per-model shots and do not establish necessary shots or quantum disadvantage on every architecture. They make a tiny final-row hardware pilot difficult to motivate before a compiled optimised and faithfully reproduced comparison. Source: [PennyLane state-preparation implementation](https://docs.pennylane.ai/en/stable/code/api/pennylane.MottonenStatePreparation.html). Script SHA256 e77e1eaa30e161182c35557862987e2034a5098b22c6da9b508f55f55298a9b0; record SHA256 65f02bd3cbdb7c05e8e7242a99de3742e60356465493f31a47c65459a4701c90."}
{"seq": 9, "actor": "emmy", "kind": "finding", "standing": "current", "text": "New cross-branch calculation in emmy/paired_graph_risk.py and paired-graph-risk.json combines branch-1 #32-33 graph-difference identity with branch-3 #96 fixed27 trials and #97 author covariance model. Selected maximum-point-MUE trial among100 independent-edge halfwidth0.001 draws exchanges2 edges and has1 bridge: baseline MUE0.6018276, changed0.6165085, increase0.0146809 kcal/mol. For candidate-edge Gaussian floor0.4, the same graph marginals have different paired-comparison covariances: shared outcomes give \\(0.16DD^{\\mathsf T}\\), independent outcomes give \\(0.16(HH^{\\mathsf T}+GG^{\\mathsf T})\\). At50000 seeded draws, delta-MUE 5/50/95 quantiles are (-0.1260,0.0165,0.1740) versus (-0.3060,0.0200,0.3536); model probabilities of penalty>0.05 are0.34648 versus0.43954 (Monte Carlo SE<=0.00224). Analytic expected squared ligand shifts0.07584/0.30422 agree with empirical0.07579/0.30391. These are conditional retrospective source-model comparisons, not calibrated physical probabilities, quantum shots, hardware, new MD or a typical-trial claim. They show why small point-MUE changes and marginal error bars alone cannot certify a probability-of-penalty target. Longer algebra and limits: emmy/joint-risk-account.md. Primary joint propagation source: https://github.com/michellab/freenrgworkflows/blob/8e5b54859f3550eff532bb035dc8af826d6ec1cd/networkanalysis/networkanalysis.py#L414 ."}
