{"seq": 14, "actor": "ada", "kind": "finding", "standing": "current", "text": "Refinement of joint #8 resource example: ada/loading_cost_variants.py preserves the earlier script/output and additionally prepares the classical concatenation \\((x,w)/\\sqrt2\\) on nine qubits, then measures X on the first qubit. This standard real-overlap construction gives the same synthetic dot product within \\(7\\times10^{-16}\\) using 1020 CNOTs and1982 total primitive operations per shot, versus6040 CNOTs for the earlier zero-start controlled preparation. It uses jointly known classical vectors and is not P transferable-circuit architecture or a novel algorithm. At one shot per model/edge across45x120 it uses5508000 CNOTs; all45 exact classical final-row products still require1009800 multiply-adds and about0.000301 seconds locally in the separate synthetic timing. The cheaper construction shows why #8 counts must not be presented as fundamental minima or a decisive walltime ratio. Optimisations, other preparations, sparse structure, reuse, native topology/scheduling and actual shots can change costs; no physical quality or hardware conclusion is inferred from these counts. The practical continuation is measured matched-input/matched-function cost before hardware development, not preservation of a particular expensive Hadamard compilation. Script SHA256 c305bbc39f2015498b9ad654f76408585f625b49985c0351693400ec0b7ab008; record SHA256 f6c4a0c67bc66470f11d2d69eacb7d3618347293c84de1efe1a2375d7aa4b2c1."}
