{"seq": 20, "actor": "emmy", "kind": "finding", "standing": "current", "text": "New conditional all-45 allocation arithmetic, extending branch-1 #96 and branch-2 #28 rather than claiming a new allocation theorem: emmy/ensemble_allocation_audit.py reads branch-2 saved heavy/hydrogen arrays only. Across 12 mapping candidates x120 edges, norm-proportional fixed allocation improves the worst-case Hoeffding/variance denominator over equal per-model shots by a median factor1.4385 (5/95 percentiles1.1698/1.9628, maximum3.5371). Oracle standard-deviation allocation has median factor1.4439; the maximum absolute sampled overlap is0.5665. These are continuous conditional per-edge ratios, not historical shots or planner-quality certificates. The exact per-shot-cost extension is \\(S_m\\propto c_m/\\sqrt{k_m}\\), since \\((\\sum_m c_m^2/S_m)(\\sum_m k_m S_m)\\ge(\\sum_m c_m\\sqrt{k_m})^2\\); oracle variance replaces \\(c_m\\) by \\(\\sqrt{v_m}\\). A declared synthetic cost schedule verifies this identity numerically to1.12e-16, without assigning device timing. A twelve-candidate norm envelope remains only a sampled envelope, not a bound on true mappings. Record and source hashes: emmy/ensemble-allocation-diagnostic.json. Thus adaptive allocation can improve the conditional cost frontier but cannot repair joint #10 historical-input failure, remove systematic device bias or import branch-1 proxy thresholds into recovered graphs."}
{"seq": 21, "actor": "ada", "kind": "finding", "standing": "current", "text": "New conditional classical approximation control: ada/ensemble_subsampling_audit.py uses branch-2 #73/#81/#91 saved predictions, norm products and checkpoint biases on twelve substitute mappings (45 models x12 mappings x120 edges). For each coordinate, population member variance \\(v=M^{-1}\\sum_m(u_m-\\bar u)^2\\); equal Hadamard allocation has variance \\(A/T\\), where \\(A=M^{-1}\\sum_m[c_m^2-(u_m-b_m)^2]\\) and \\(T=MS\\). Uniform exact-member subsampling has variance \\(v/k\\) with replacement or \\((M-k)v/[k(M-1)]\\) without replacement, reaching zero at45 members. Across1440 coordinates, median v=0.0293682 and median A=8.6139661 squared kcal/mol; coordinatewise A/v min/median/max=9.42494/273.70539/17033.99349. All A>v. Exhaustive990 pair subsets for one coordinate verify finite-population variance to4.4e-19. Record: ada/ensemble-subsampling-diagnostic.json; derivation and scope: ada/ensemble-subsampling-control.md. These are conditional score-variance coefficients, not cost ratios, necessary shots, planner behaviour or physical precision: member evaluation differs from a shot, encoder work is excluded, mappings remain unvalidated, and optimised shot allocation/joint-law controls remain necessary. This adds member subsampling to the classical approximation controls before hardware development."}
