{"seq": 4, "actor": "ada", "kind": "finding", "standing": "corrected by #47; not cited by the joint ledger", "text": "Supported algebraic consequence of entry 3: for a real nonzero input, the exact noiseless P output is \\(f_\\theta(x)=\\hat x^\\mathsf{T}w(\\theta)+b\\), where \\(\\hat x=x/\\|x\\|_2\\), \\(w(\\theta)=\\operatorname{Re}[U_\\theta|0\\rangle]\\), and \\(\\|w(\\theta)\\|_2\\leq1\\). Thus a classical circuit-state parameterisation with the same angles and analytic differentiation is an exact function and gradient comparator before transfer. A free classical filter after transfer relaxes this parameterisation; subsequent learning need not follow the same optimiser trajectory. For Q an unnormalised dense neuron \\(a^\\mathsf{T}x+b\\) requires restoring both norms, or explicitly retraining a different normalised architecture. The small P filter permits computing four amplitudes once per parameter update and all 15 binary-pattern outputs by classical dot products. This does not prove every large weight circuit is efficiently simulable, but eliminates an inference-function expressivity advantage and supplies a mandatory comparator for this proposed dense-head application."}
{"seq": 5, "actor": "ada", "kind": "correction", "standing": "corrected by #46; not cited by the joint ledger", "text": "Refinement of the scan rationale, not a contradiction of Q: reciprocal plus min-max scaling cannot itself amplify rank errors while SEM estimates remain strictly positive and extrema are distinct. The score is a common strictly decreasing function \\(s(u)=(1/u-1/u_{\\max})/(1/u_{\\min}-1/u_{\\max})\\), hence \\(s(u_i)>s(u_j)\\iff u_i<u_j\\). Extrema matter for absolute score thresholds and therefore potentially for LOMAP topology, but not for ordering alone. The precision question must specify whether the planner uses ordering, numeric thresholds, or both. Degenerate extrema and noisy zero/negative predictions need an explicit handling rule. Q input/Q.txt:393-424 gives the transform; its actual planner implementation must be checked before attributing fragility to the reciprocal."}
