{"seq": 9, "actor": "ada", "kind": "finding", "standing": "current; not cited by the joint ledger", "text": "Resource derivation for the narrow final-neuron substitution, assuming known classical norm product \\(c_e=\\|x_e\\|_2\\|a\\|_2\\), independent unbiased Hadamard shots \\(Z\\in\\{-1,1\\}\\), exact state preparation and no hardware bias: \\(\\hat u_e=b+c_e\\bar Z_e\\), \\(\\operatorname{Var}(\\hat u_e)=c_e^2(1-h_e^2)/S_e\\). Hoeffding and a union bound over \\(E\\) edges give radii \\(r_e=c_e\\sqrt{2\\log(2E/\\alpha)/S_e}\\). A comparison is certified only when the SEM confidence intervals are disjoint; exact ties need a policy. For equal \\(c\\), preserving all distinct-value orders separated by \\(\\Delta\\) is sufficiently guaranteed by \\(S>8c^2\\log(2E/\\alpha)/\\Delta^2\\). Using entry 8 smallest positive gap, \\(E=120\\), \\(\\alpha=0.05\\), and a purely illustrative \\(c=1\\) kcal/mol gives about 80.4 billion shots per edge. This is an over-stringent sufficient bound, NOT an observed requirement, NOT a lower bound, and NOT a network-quality certificate; actual norms are unavailable and LOMAP may never compare the closest pair. Its purpose is to reject uniform all-ranking preservation as the experimental objective and require planner-specific decisive comparisons."}
{"seq": 10, "actor": "ada", "kind": "objection", "standing": "corrected by #47; unanswered; not cited by the joint ledger", "text": "Further consequence of entries 4 and 6: a P-style amplitude circuit on \\(q=\\lceil\\log_2 d\\rceil\\) data qubits has a classical state vector of only \\(2^q<2d\\) amplitudes. A gate-local circuit of \\(G\\) gates is classically evaluable in \\(O(Gd)\\) time and \\(O(d)\\) space, once per row and parameter update, followed by ordinary batched dot products. This is polynomial in dense-layer input size, even if the circuit entangles every data qubit. Q final row has 128 complex amplitudes (2048 bytes at complex128); 700 first-head-row states of length 1024 occupy 11.47 MB in decimal units, excluding autodiff buffers. Three P-style layers would have 63 final-row angles versus 100 unconstrained Q weights, or 90 angles per first-head row versus 905 weights. Therefore such a replacement changes parameterisation unless expressivity is established. Quantum shot noise may still affect optimisation or act as regularisation, but that claim requires matched circuit-parameter classical training, noise controls and costs; it cannot be credited to an unavailable classical function or generic square-matrix speedup."}
