{"seq": 7, "actor": "ada", "kind": "finding", "standing": "corrected by #13; corrected by #15; corrected by #20; not cited by the joint ledger", "text": "Q artefacts are recoverable at snapshot e164147909fef7c1d810ccb3ab76a5f7a24f0fb7, with limitations. Tree lists TYK2 compiled MBAR values, experimental data, fully connected CSVs, saved prediction CSVs tyk2_0 through tyk2_8 and TensorFlow checkpoints. Checkpoint bytes have not been downloaded or loaded. Recovered _01_twin_gcn.py:418-449 gives 450 features per ligand, 5 mapping features, then dense widths 700,450,100,1: the combined vector has dimension 905. _04_external_test_all_series.py:450-491 loads per-replicate groups of 5 folds and averages each group; lines 1029-1041 write one prediction CSV per group. This supports 9 groups of 5 folds, but missing-fold exceptions and subsequent aggregation still need auditing. Sources: [Q model construction](https://github.com/michellab/RBFENN/blob/e164147909fef7c1d810ccb3ab76a5f7a24f0fb7/ANALYSIS/perturbation_networks/_01_twin_gcn.py), [Q ensemble loader](https://github.com/michellab/RBFENN/blob/e164147909fef7c1d810ccb3ab76a5f7a24f0fb7/ANALYSIS/perturbation_networks/_04_external_test_all_series.py), [Q TYK2 data directory](https://github.com/michellab/RBFENN/tree/e164147909fef7c1d810ccb3ab76a5f7a24f0fb7/ANALYSIS/perturbation_networks/input/testsets/tyk2)."}
{"seq": 8, "actor": "emmy", "kind": "finding", "standing": "corrected by #15; not cited by the joint ledger", "text": "Recovered TYK2 decision inputs, not a proposed measurement: nine saved files output/series_predictions/tyk2_0.csv through tyk2_8.csv each contain 240 rows with matching edge keys and duplicated reverse directions, giving 120 undirected edges. Averaging pred_sem_mean over the nine files and applying reciprocal/min-max scaling reproduces process/lomap/lomap_inputs_pred_sems.csv with maximum absolute discrepancy 1.1102230246251565e-16. SEM range is 0.05104393044444445 to 0.6855965633333333 kcal/mol; four adjacent gaps are exactly zero; minimum positive gap is 7.40044444444421e-06 and median adjacent gap 0.0022151944444444016 kcal/mol. These are complete-order gaps, NOT active network-decision margins or observed quality loss. Primary sources: [saved TYK2 replicate 0](https://github.com/michellab/RBFENN/blob/e164147909fef7c1d810ccb3ab76a5f7a24f0fb7/ANALYSIS/perturbation_networks/output/series_predictions/tyk2_0.csv), [saved LOMAP inputs](https://github.com/michellab/RBFENN/blob/e164147909fef7c1d810ccb3ab76a5f7a24f0fb7/ANALYSIS/perturbation_networks/process/lomap/lomap_inputs_pred_sems.csv). emmy/margin-results.json records the calculation. Q _06 notebook source extraction :51-71 averages replicate fold means and optionally clips percentiles; saved inputs match UNCLIPPED reconstruction. Q loadEnsemble :455-458 computes n_replicates=max(parsed ids) then range(n_replicates), so indexed model set and actual loader must be audited rather than inferred from the prose 9/45 count. Checkpoint .data/.index files ARE listed in the tree; the absence of .h5 is not absence of weights."}
{"seq": 9, "actor": "ada", "kind": "finding", "standing": "corrected by #13; corrected by #15; corrected by #20; not cited by the joint ledger", "text": "Executable audit ada/interface_audit.py and results ada/interface_audit_results.json verify that the recovered TYK2 CSV has 240 directed rows, 16 nodes and exactly antisymmetric free energies with identical reverse errors: 120 unique pairs, no independent reverse MD. Under the assumption of 45 complete models, replacing the entire recovered Q head requires 6,755,400 overlap estimates per 120-pair prediction pass, before shots, state preparation, gradients or transfer; its ordinary dense arithmetic is 993,600 multiply-accumulates per edge/model. Replacing only the last scalar row needs 5,400 overlaps and seven working qubits (128 amplitudes). These are forward arithmetic counts, not timings. Repo files are linked in #7; the FC CSV source is [TYK2 fully connected results](https://github.com/michellab/RBFENN/blob/e164147909fef7c1d810ccb3ab76a5f7a24f0fb7/ANALYSIS/perturbation_networks/input/testsets/tyk2/fep_data_tyk2_fc.csv)."}
{"seq": 10, "actor": "ada", "kind": "idea", "standing": "corrected by #13; corrected by #20; corrected by #34; not cited by the joint ledger", "text": "Sharper contribution candidate: a decision-quality versus total-cost frontier for transferable quantum weight-state RBFE predictors, with a matched CLASSICAL circuit-parameterisation comparator. A final scalar Q head has only 128 padded amplitudes, so explicit classical local-gate state-vector evolution and exact overlap training are practical comparators in principle. P extraction need not form the full unitary: evolving its initial basis vector gives its first column. Same circuit parameters, norm restoration, optimiser effort and noise law must match before any effect is attributed to quantum execution. Classical continuation changes parameter coordinates and may expand the reachable weight manifold; equality at handoff does not imply equal subsequent optimisation. Derivation and assumptions in ada/transfer_frontier.md. This sharpens the scan precision proposal rather than asserting a new quantum algorithm or publication novelty."}
{"seq": 11, "actor": "emmy", "kind": "idea", "standing": "corrected by #37; not cited by the joint ledger", "text": "Sharpened question and supported bound are in emmy/precision-bound.md: use a frozen final scalar dense layer first, restoring both vector norms, to separate interface error from training-path changes. For ideal independent shots, ordinary dense output variance is at most the squared product of input and weight norms divided by shot count. An equally weighted R-model ensemble with equal per-model shots S and norm products bounded by A has simultaneous M-edge error at most eta with probability at least 1-delta if \\(RS\\ge 2A^2\\eta^{-2}\\log(2M/\\delta)\\). Ensemble averaging reduces shots PER model, not this sufficient TOTAL shot bound. Correlated bias is excluded. Edge comparison gaps give sufficient rank certificates; exact rank preservation is unnecessary for physical quality. Q saved complete-order ties/gaps (#8) therefore do not determine a required hardware shot count. The executable audit is emmy/audit_margins.py, run successfully with uv and only the Python standard library. A replay must identify active selector decisions, test changed graphs using fixed FC edge data and the identical weighted regression, and evaluate per-ligand MUE at matched edge/sampling budget. The classical state-vector/amplitude comparator in Ada #5 is mandatory. No finite-shot training, noise benefit, physical improvement or speedup is observed here."}
{"seq": 12, "actor": "ada", "kind": "finding", "standing": "corrected by #17; corrected by #20; not cited by the joint ledger", "text": "Supported derivation for a restored ordinary dense output: for ideal independent ancilla shots, \\(\\operatorname{Var}(\\widehat z)=\\|x\\|_2^2\\|w\\|_2^2(1-h^2)/S\\). This is conditional on fixed parameters and exact real weight-state preparation. A fixed P-style three-layer circuit on the seven working qubits of Q final head has 63 angles; even adding a scalar weight scale cannot span every arbitrary 100-entry weight row. Thus an exact original-model substitution needs a more expressive preparation, while a fixed shallow replacement must be treated as a changed trainable parameterisation. A classical circuit-parameterisation baseline separates that restriction from measurement noise. See ada/transfer_frontier.md, exact-function and smallest-test sections; no latent norms, circuit-trained RBFE model or shots-to-MUE curve were measured."}
{"seq": 13, "actor": "emmy", "kind": "correction", "standing": "corrected by #17; corrected by #20; corrected by #35; corrected by #36; not cited by the joint ledger", "text": "Correction to the applicability of widths in Emmy #6 and Ada #7/#9/#10: those are the PRETRAINING head. Primary _02_transfer_learn_sem.py:95-129 chooses base_model.layers[-4].output (the 700-unit layer), so it RETAINS that layer and appends int-linspace widths 560,373,187,1. _04_external_test_all_series.py:976-982 calls modelTransfer(fepnn,4,4) before loading finetuned checkpoints. Static recovered construction therefore has widths 905,700,560,373,187,1. It entails 1,304,318 dense MACs per edge/model and 9,833,400 overlaps for the whole head over 120 edges and 45 complete models; a final scalar substitution still needs 5,400 overlaps but 187 input coordinates padded to 256, i.e. 8 working qubits plus ancilla, not 7. Checkpoint loading and model summaries remain unexecuted, so these are static-construction counts conditional on standard Keras layer ordering. Source: [Q transfer-head construction](https://github.com/michellab/RBFENN/blob/e164147909fef7c1d810ccb3ab76a5f7a24f0fb7/ANALYSIS/perturbation_networks/_02_transfer_learn_sem.py). The first 905-to-700 overlap count in #6 remains applicable to the retained layer."}
{"seq": 14, "actor": "emmy", "kind": "objection", "standing": "answered by #31; answered by #64; not cited by the joint ledger", "text": "Remaining limit on the precision candidate: exact Q-era Cresset LOMAP implementation and version-specific decision path were not recovered here; the notebook delegates to BioSimSpace Align.generateNetwork with user links and commented-out forced edge count (_06 source :405-410). Current public LOMAP would not automatically validate that historical selection. No active selector margin, latent input/weight norm, graph perturbation replay, hardware compilation, gradient cost, or target-held-out result has been measured. Reciprocal scaling preserves order for positive inputs, so the scan claim about amplification needs qualification: thresholds/extrema can matter, but amplification is not by itself a rank-instability argument. A rank-only spanning-tree replay would be an alternative planner experiment, not a reproduction of Q. The retrieved nine scalar prediction arrays permit an input-level decision audit; they do not determine the quantum noise distribution in the learnt latent layers."}
{"seq": 15, "actor": "ada", "kind": "correction", "standing": "current; not cited by the joint ledger", "text": "Clarification to #7/#9 ensemble assumptions, independently cross-checked against the recovered Git tree: it lists 50 finetuned checkpoint pairs, replicate IDs 0 through 9 each with folds 0 through 4. The loader sets n_replicates=max(ids) then iterates range(n_replicates), excluding ID 9 and yielding 9 groups/45 candidate models when all load. The saved TYK2 files 0 through 8 align with that behaviour. Thus 45-model forward counts in #9 describe the apparent released inference path, not all available checkpoint files; checkpoint loading and paper-run provenance remain unverified. Manifest ada/recovery_manifest.json hashes the downloaded source/data bytes. Emmy #8 confirms the saved-score aggregation separately."}
{"seq": 16, "actor": "ada", "kind": "finding", "standing": "corrected by #34; not cited by the joint ledger", "text": "Closing account: supported source recovery establishes normalised-input transfer, analytic simulator execution and classical full-unitary extraction in P, plus ordinary dense heads and recoverable TYK2 retrospective data in Q. Executable audit establishes dimensions, duplicated reverse data and forward operation counts; the shallow weight-state model-class obstruction is a derivation, not an observed failure. I independently checked Emmy #11 Hoeffding form: for independent bounded contributions to a mean over R models and S shots per model, its sufficient RS bound follows by a union bound over M edges, assuming the stated common norm-product bound. This does not give an actual required shot number and excludes correlated bias. The concrete continuation is a frozen scalar-head precision/transfer study with a matched classical circuit-parameterisation control, retrospective per-ligand MUE and full cost accounting. Unresolved: actual checkpoint loading and latent norms, archived selector implementation/active margins, hardware preparation/extraction/gradient costs, target-held-out physical validation and publication novelty. No MD, network-quality result, quantum advantage or scientific verdict is awarded."}
