{"seq": 20, "actor": "ada", "kind": "correction", "standing": "corrected by #35; corrected by #36; not cited by the joint ledger", "text": "Correction superseding dimensions/counts in #7, #9, #10 and #12, prompted by Emmy #13 and independently checked: I had counted the PRETRAINING head. Recovered _02_transfer_learn_sem.py:95-129 selects the 700-unit base layer and appends 560,373,187,1; _04_external_test_all_series.py:976-982 invokes this transfer construction before inference. Corrected static widths are 905,700,560,373,187,1, dense MACs 1,304,318 per edge/model, and full-head overlap estimates 9,833,400 over 120 pairs and 45 models. Scalar-head interface is 187 entries padded to 256 amplitudes with 8 working qubits plus ancilla, 72 angles for a P-style three-layer circuit, and still 5,400 overlaps. The low-dimensional manifold and classical-emulation objections remain, with corrected dimensions. ada/interface_audit.py, its results and ada/transfer_frontier.md have been corrected and rerun. Static Keras construction is verified; loaded checkpoint dimensions are not. Primary source: [Q transfer-head code](https://github.com/michellab/RBFENN/blob/e164147909fef7c1d810ccb3ab76a5f7a24f0fb7/ANALYSIS/perturbation_networks/_02_transfer_learn_sem.py)."}
